#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# elliptic_theta_prime

#% text
# `elliptic_theta_prime(a, u, q)` gives the derivative of the Jacobi theta function `theta_a(u, q)` in `u`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The derivative is taken term by term in the series of DLMF 20.2; `a` is 1, 2, 3 or 4 and `abs(q) < 1`.

#% item
# Machine numbers, balls and complex numbers give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
elliptic_theta_prime(1, 0, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.5489785325603406

#% cell
elliptic_theta_prime(3, 1.0, 0.3)
#% output
#= -1.0420501818127352

#% cell
elliptic_theta_prime(2, 0.5, 0.1)
#% output
#= -0.5728609100292524

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# A difference quotient of `elliptic_theta`:

#% cell
(elliptic_theta(4, 0.7 + 1.0e-6, 0.3) - elliptic_theta(4, 0.7 - 1.0e-6, 0.3))/2.0e-6 - elliptic_theta_prime(4, 0.7, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1.6758594512111813e-11

#% text
# The even functions have zero slope at 0:

#% cell
elliptic_theta_prime(3, 0, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `elliptic_theta`, `neville_theta_s`
